#
# Phase 4 LAN-access image: the phase4-complete image with the exposure-scope fix.
#
# Why this image exists at all.
#
# Publishing the WebUI on a LAN address invalidated one premise the runtime held:
# `/metrics` was served without a session to any caller with a private peer address,
# on the reasoning — written into the code — that the container publishes on loopback
# only. Behind a published port every external caller arrives from the Docker bridge
# gateway, which is itself RFC1918, so that predicate says "trusted" for a LAN client
# exactly as readily as for a host-local one. Correct while the publish was
# 127.0.0.1; false the moment it was not.
#
# The fix is source-only and lives in services/reference-control-plane/src/. The
# running container executes the code baked into its image, so the fix could not
# reach the installation without a new image.
#
# Why an overlay rather than a rebuild from oci/Dockerfile — the same reasoning
# Dockerfile.phase4 recorded, and it has not changed:
#
#   * oci/Dockerfile runs `apt-get install`, which needs the Debian archives. This
#     gate authorises no network operation, and repeating the apt step would silently
#     re-resolve the OS package set to whatever the archive serves today.
#   * Building FROM the audited phase4-complete image inherits every layer unchanged —
#     PostgreSQL 18.4, pgvector 0.8.5, the whole apt set — so the only difference
#     between the two images is two first-party source files.
#
# Stated rather than hidden: this image's lineage is
# node:22-bookworm-slim@sha256:6c74791e… -> :phase3 -> :phase4 -> :phase4-complete ->
# :phase4-complete-lan, so it carries all of their layers. Phase 5 packaging should
# still rebuild from oci/Dockerfile with a recorded network step (D-0033).
#
# Build offline, and only offline:
#   docker build --network=none --pull=false \
#     -f oci/Dockerfile.phase4-complete-lan \
#     -t noesar-evolution:phase4-complete-lan .
ARG BASE_IMAGE=noesar-evolution:phase4-complete
FROM ${BASE_IMAGE}

LABEL org.opencontainers.image.version="1.0.0-ai-workspace-phase4-complete-lan"
LABEL org.noesar.phase="4-complete-lan"
LABEL org.noesar.base-image="noesar-evolution:phase4-complete"
LABEL org.noesar.phase4.lan-remediations="F4L-001"
LABEL org.noesar.exposure.default="loopback"

USER root
# Exactly the two files that changed. Copying the whole service tree would make the
# diff between this image and its base unreviewable, which is the opposite of why an
# overlay was chosen.
COPY --chown=10001:10001 services/reference-control-plane/src/http-security.mjs \
     /opt/noesar/services/reference-control-plane/src/http-security.mjs
COPY --chown=10001:10001 services/reference-control-plane/src/server.mjs \
     /opt/noesar/services/reference-control-plane/src/server.mjs
USER 10001:10001
